Synthesis of N-(4-fluorophenyl)benzenesulfonamide (22): | The reaction was carried out according to the general procedure A for 8 h, using benzenesulfonamide (78 mg, 0.5 mmol), 1-chloro-4- fluorobenzene (98 mg, 0.75 mmol), K2CO3 (104 mg, 0.75 mmol), Fe(acac)3 (9 mg, 5 mol%), CuI (5 mg, 5 mol%) and DMSO (100 µl per 0.5 mmol scale of reaction). After silica gel column chromatography (16% ethyl acetate in hexane), the title compound (98 mg, 78% yield) was obtained as a white solid. 7 White solid; mp 130-132 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.81 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 7.74 (s, 1H), 7.54 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.43 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.13-7.09 (m, 2H), 6.93-6.89 (m, 2H);
